# TEMPLATE — not applied, not encrypted, not read by anything. It exists so the
# shape of the real file is reviewable in git while the real file is opaque
# ciphertext. Copy it to `pve-token.sops.yaml`, fill the one placeholder,
# encrypt with `sops -e -i`, and commit the encrypted result alongside this
# template (which stays, as the diffable reference).
#
# The value is the secret half of the PVE API token minted by
# scripts/mint-pve-monitoring-token.sh — a bare UUID, e.g.
# 8f4c1d2e-3a5b-4c6d-9e0f-1a2b3c4d5e6f. The other two halves of the credential,
# PVE_USER (monitoring@pve) and PVE_TOKEN_NAME (prometheus), are not secrets and
# are set in plaintext in ./pve-exporter-deployment.yaml.
#
# ⚠ Keep the quotes. A UUID happens to survive unquoted because it contains
# letters and dashes, but the rule this repo enforces is unconditional: a SOPS
# value entered without quotes re-encrypts with `type:int` (or `type:bool`) in
# the ciphertext envelope, and a Kubernetes Secret's stringData is
# map[string]string. Nothing in the pipeline notices — the file is valid YAML,
# kustomize builds it, kubeconform validates the Secret — and it fails only at
# Argo sync time with "cannot unmarshal number into Go struct field
# Secret.stringData of type string", leaving every *other* resource in the
# overlay applied and just this one Secret missing. CI greps for the type tag.
#
# ⚠ This file's name matters twice over. ../../../../.sops.yaml matches
# `clusters/.*\.sops\.ya?ml$` with `encrypted_regex: ^(data|stringData)$`, so
# only the payload is encrypted and metadata stays diffable — a differently
# named file would encrypt whole and stop being reviewable. And
# ./secret-generator.yaml lists `pve-token.sops.yaml` by that exact name: until
# the encrypted file exists at that path the ksops generator cannot resolve it
# and the whole monitoring overlay fails to render in the repo-server. The
# `.example` suffix is what keeps *this* file out of both CI's sops type check
# (`find clusters -name '*.sops.yaml'`) and its direct-CR kubeconform lint
# (`find clusters -name '*.yaml'`); neither pattern matches it.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: pve-exporter-token
  namespace: monitoring
type: Opaque
stringData:
  PVE_TOKEN_VALUE: "<paste-uuid-here>"
